WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
Lift a weight, or stretch a spring.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.330
The work you do is stored,
ready to come back.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:12.140
Now someone hands you just one thing: a
graph of that stored energy at each position.

4
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.270
No force arrows.

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.450
No formula.

6
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.030
Only the energy.

7
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.400
From that graph alone, could you
work out the force on the object,

8
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.950
wherever it is?

9
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.670
In this mission, you'll find the work
done by a force that fades as it pushes,

10
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.050
and see why the starting force times
the distance gives the wrong answer.

11
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.910
Then you'll find out which
forces can store energy,

12
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.080
and why friction never can.

13
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.350
Your mission: find out whether stored
energy alone reveals the force,

14
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.990
and if it does, how.
